{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/83065-cover-questions","id":83065,"title":"Cover Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-03T03:13:54-08:00","id":83065,"title":"Cover Questions","content":"I feel I have a wrong view on how cover works and how vulnerable cover really is. So if anyone can clear this up I would be grateful. Thanks in advance.<br /> <br /> <br /> How does one create a pact without damaging or risking your cover? It seems like if anyone learns you are a demon for any reason it is a compromise. If your character does something out of character they take a compromise roll. Since people don't go around offering pacts that seems out of cover and would be another compromise roll.<br /> <br /> Cultist (5 dot) makes the cultist well aware of the demons nature and the nature of the god machine. Unless the demon is completely disconnect everyone in the cult would know the demon is a demon and if they where ever made aware of the demons cover it would be crippled by the amount of compromise rolls they would take.<br /> <br /> Since all it takes is belief that the demons cover is not natural to break a cover why doesn't the god machine suspicious of a cover test it by sending an angel to tell their cultist Hey this guy is a demon, and once those cultist believe that they will cause a wave of compromise rolls breaking apart a cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T06:04:03-08:00","id":83123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/83065-cover-questions#post83065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel I have a wrong view on how cover works and how vulnerable cover really is. So if anyone can clear this up I would be grateful. Thanks in advance.<br /> <br /> <br /> How does one create a pact without damaging or risking your cover? It seems like if anyone learns you are a demon for any reason it is a compromise. If your character does something out of character they take a compromise roll. Since people don't go around offering pacts that seems out of cover and would be another compromise roll.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, haven't you ever heard of stories of some shady mafia bookie who takes your sister in payment for your debts? Or any kind of human trafficking, for that matter? Demons may not be evil spirits, but they ARE involved with criminals. So it shouldn't be too much a shock to find some like that among their kind. <br /> <br /> Or how about an information broker, who trades information in exchange for &quot;introductions&quot; to other people? I'm sure that one could twist the wording of the pact document to make &quot;introduction&quot; into &quot;I take your place.&quot;<br /> <br /> These methods don't force one to reveal a demonic nature, nor to act out of cover. I'm sure there's other ways as well. Its not easy, but its possible. After all, there's a -reason- that Tempters are well respected and known for being in the Cover trading business. They're the ones who specialize in arranging for these kinds of pacts.<br /> <br /> Soul pacts need to be signed in blood - nothing stops you from filling an ink pen with blood. <br /> <br /> Cults are nice, since as a member / leader, its easy to arrange things for someone to sign a document without causing a compromise roll, since doing that is 1) part of the cult's Cover, and 2) generally free from needing to see a demonic explanation. Plus, aren't these kinds of organizations known for having people entering them signing away everything they have? Not hard to add a bit more, like familial relations. <br /> <br /> So, if you don't have some kind of reason to be going up to people with pacts, then yeah, its hard and will likely call for compromises. That said, most demons lay ground work of some kind, or get involved with others that do. Then, its much easier.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cultist (5 dot) makes the cultist well aware of the demons nature and the nature of the god machine. Unless the demon is completely disconnect everyone in the cult would know the demon is a demon and if they where ever made aware of the demons cover it would be crippled by the amount of compromise rolls they would take. </div> </div> </div> Cover 5 says a few people are aware of it, and are stigmatics. Only a chosen few know the absolute truth. Even if it wasn't, groups count only as a single compromise roll, not mulitple. Besides, -why- are you trusting everyone with that much information? You can't trust them! How do you know they're not rival demons? Or angelic cultists hunting you? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since all it takes is belief that the demons cover is not natural to break a cover why doesn't the god machine suspicious of a cover test it by sending an angel to tell their cultist Hey this guy is a demon, and once those cultist believe that they will cause a wave of compromise rolls breaking apart a cover. </div> </div> </div> One, its not that easy to simply send angels anywhere. That requires a summoning ritual &quot;occult matrix.&quot; <br /> <br /> Two, if God knew enough to suspect one person, their Cover would be shredded and hunter angels on their way. Demons aren't so casual as to be easily suspected by the God Machine - those that are end up dead. What would that demon be doing where the God Machine would know? I can't even imagine the situation where someone still has a cover up and running, and has been pegged as a demon by the GM.<br /> <br /> Three, I'm fairly sure it has to be absolute proof / truth revealed at some point, and not just a rumor that's being spread. Otherwise... People will quickly lose faith in an angelic being that goes around and casually does hit/miss, and stop believing anything it says. When a cultist starts thinking an angel is testing them instead of revealing absolute truth, there goes the entire point of the exercise. Worse, the angel has no way of knowing when this happens, making it an unreliable method, even if it could be done. <br /> <br /> Four, cultists shredding someone's Cover already has mechanics - the investigation. THAT is what they do when they have a suspicion. Simply saying that someone is suspicious would negate the need for that mechanic.<br /> <br /> Five, its not &quot;belief the cover is not natural.&quot; Its that you've had a key fact of your existence revealed to someone and the person didn't brush you off. Its not so much belief that matters as &quot;accepting this as fact.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T08:13:52-08:00","id":83178,"title":"","content":"Once you mentioned absolute truth being a factor it reminded me of that embed that only works on hidden object and not just object you can't find. The full matter is looked at when dealings with compromises not just the result. So an angel would need to believe they are propagating the truth when they speak to others to trigger a compromise and also the situation and group would need to be different for each compromise roll.Thanks for clearing that up for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}